{
  "content": "The standalone retrieval service stores documentation in PostgreSQL using the pgvector extension. During ingestion, documents are divided into overlapping chunks and encoded with a local embedding model. When a client submits a question, the service combines vector similarity with keyword search to find relevant chunks. An optional local cross-encoder can rerank those candidates before they are returned. Each returned chunk includes its content, title, citation label, chunk identifier, and available source URL. The service does not generate answers. Clients such as a local language model or the VS Code knowledge extension use the retrieved context to compose an answer. Configuration is loaded from environment variables and the .env file.",
  "title": "Standalone retrieval overview",
  "metadata": {
    "author": "team"
  }
}

